Subject: Cantor Seeded Compiler Slice 4 External Inference Host Activation Review

@ [review_uuid] fc7bbf00-0bb8-4c6b-a8c1-0d270f91e17b
@ [source_uuid] bfaa7604-0ee4-4fb7-acf5-8b02574d2af2

& [Delineation]
  + compilation produces an inert integration candidate while execution launches providers tools and processes only after separate verification and admission
  + external OpenAI-compatible provider transport MCP tool transport and Cantor semantic procedure are separate identities
  + buffered multi-pass reentry is supported while mid-completion hidden-state or semantic insertion is not claimed
  + internal llama.cpp extension is a different target requiring limitation evidence and cannot substitute for this external adapter

& [SpecificationJustificationSolution]
  + [source] preserved user three-level compiler intent and existing external-loop evidence are explicit
  + [justification] the external loop already proves the lowest-risk host shape and should become a typed replayable artifact before new runtime code exists
  + [solution_boundary] strict candidate forms and pure projection only

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + HostImplementationPin owns adapter identity revision content digest and configuration profile
  + ProviderProtocolBinding owns provider family protocol endpoint policy model selector request profile and observed capability set
  + ModelToolBinding owns exact advertised schema result contract and digest
  + McpProcessBinding owns executable configuration transport operation and digest identities
  + HostFlowContract owns ordered stages pass and call limits concurrency cancellation streaming time and output bounds
  + CompatibilityAccount owns controls observations limitations and rollback without claiming successful execution
  + InferenceHostIntegrationCandidate owns all pins upstream lineage unresolved non-authority and digest

& [DualHemisphereThinking]
  + [divergent] direct llama.cpp patch dynamic tool injection shared token stream arbitrary provider plugin and generic agent runtime were considered
  + [convergent] one buffered two-pass external adapter candidate best matches current evidence and preserves replaceable providers
  + [holistic] the candidate makes the complete seam inspectable without collapsing semantic compilation runtime execution or model internals

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + Honesty distinguishes declared compatibility observed compatibility and unmeasured behavior and forbids hidden-state claims
  + Security pins loopback policy exact code schema configuration bounds cancellation rollback and target identity
  + Weaver joins typed SOP IR attention procedure tool MCP transport provider protocol and reentry result
  + Planner orders initial pass call validation dispatch reentry final validation cancellation and stop
  + Refiner reuses the existing runner as evidence while adding no runtime behavior and keeping internal modification locked
  + Scribe records all revisions digests schemas limits observations residuals and non-authority
  + Observer closes only after positive negative compatibility and whole-workspace evidence agree

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + every preserved IntegrationCandidate statement maps to IHB-001 through IHB-009 in the Slice4 matrix
  + exact external target and internal escalation separation are acceptance-critical

& [RiskReview]
  + endpoint text alone is insufficient because host source model tool configuration and provider protocol may drift independently
  + claiming streaming when only buffered responses were tested would misrepresent the seam
  + future runtime capabilities must not be laundered into compilation-time capabilities
  + using the experimental report as admission evidence without a separate verifier remains forbidden

& [Decision]
  + activate strict pure external inference-host integration candidate forms only
  + leave the current reflection loop source and behavior unchanged
